   "place_default": "all",
   "note": "Strength runs to 6 here; the Core Collection stops at 1.5. Up to 1 the direction is taken out, from 1 to 2 it is turned round, and past 2 the sound is pushed further to the far side. Taking a direction out pulls a sound toward the middle of that direction, so a sound far along it changes most: on Deep techno, Pulse at strength 1 took the centroid from 69 Hz to 902 Hz, while on the Warm drone, which sits a little to the dark side of Brightness, Brightness at 1 raised it from 138 to 191 Hz. Almost all of the writing along Brightness and Pulse is done in block 0 and blocks 9 to 11, so on a single block in between the unit changes little; it starts on all blocks, flat, with Keep size off. Its MLX version (vau.mlx) keeps it on the GPU, so on a host that runs in MLX all twelve blocks cost no more than none."
